From: canoziia <canoziia@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] glm5next: expose DFlash aux hidden states across PP

Glm5Next lacked the EAGLE3/DFlash target interface, so a DFlash2 drafter
could not start on it. Add SupportsEagle3 + EagleModelMixin to the NVIDIA
Glm5Next target, capture the drafter's aux layers (stream_mean of the mHC
streams by default; VLLM_GLM5_AUX_HIDDEN_TENSOR=branch selects the branch
output), pack/relay/collect them over pipeline parallelism, and keep the
target input embedding on the last PP rank where the drafter lives.
Required for DFlash2 under PP; no change without a drafter.

